<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Copyright (C) 2026 SkapaCraft <https://skapacraft.com>
  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

  Entitlements for macOS builds distributed outside the Mac App Store, which
  is what tauri.conf.json points at. One entitlement, and no App Sandbox.

  The sandbox is deliberately absent here. It is mandatory on the Mac App
  Store and nowhere else, and it cannot be had without also granting
  com.apple.security.network.client, because WKWebView refuses to start
  without it (see entitlements-appstore.plist, which records the measurement).
  Applying it to a build that is not going to the Store would therefore buy a
  network permission this build has no reason to hold. Hardened runtime, set
  in tauri.conf.json, is what notarisation actually requires.

  files.user-selected.read-write covers every file access the application
  makes: the Takeout source and the destination for repaired copies both come
  from the system's own Open/Save panel, never from a path the application
  guesses or remembers. No app-scoped bookmark entitlement is requested
  because no path is kept past the session that chose it.

  There is no network entitlement here, and on this build that is not merely a
  statement of intent: nothing in the dependency graph can open a connection,
  and nothing in the sandbox would permit one.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
